{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/472827-2e-rites-questions","id":472827,"title":"[2E] Rites questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-08T08:37:45-07:00","id":472827,"title":"[2E] Rites questions","content":"Hi! Paging through the my copy of 1st edition, I noticed that rites are completely different now. So I've got some questions, maybe the devs/writers or someone knowledgeable enough could answer them:<br /> <br /> 1) Both Rite of Dedication and Rite of the Spirit Brand are no longer a thing since they are now natural capabilities of the Uratha, right?<br /> <br /> 2) Is there still a Rite of Initiation? What about that rite for renouncing a tribe? <br /> <br /> 3) Is there a rite for joining a pack now? Is there anything in particular the prospective pack member must do to get the benefits of the pack totem?<br /> <br /> That's all. Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:00:31-07:00","id":472884,"title":"","content":"You are right is saying that Rites have changed almost completely. They're not tied to Renown or Harmony in any way anymore and you get to come up with the in-game hows of the Rite yourself so long as they ping a handful of guidelines. They're a lot of fun.<br /> <br /> As to your questions, yeah, none of those are Rites, per se anymore. The Rite of Dedication is subsumed into &quot;Werewolves with good Harmony can do this, werewolves with bad Harmony cannot&quot;. The Spirit Brand thing is actually done by the Lunes themselves. (Not sure how the Pure do it...)<br /> As to Initiation and Renunciation, mostly Rites left in the game are things they want people spending XP on and then using with some regularity. Leaving a tribe or joining a new one do not fall under that purview.<br /> Pack initiation could be a zero-dot rite if you wanted. Just pick something and say that's how it's done. For new members to get the totem benefit, they should take a dot of the Totem Merit. (This last point is somewhat debatable as humans can't take the Merit, but it does say somewhere that they get the Totem boon benefit. Any takers on this one?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:15:53-07:00","id":472892,"title":"","content":"I forgot to add my fourth:<br /> <br /> 4) There is no Rite of Healing anymore. How do Uratha heal Aggravated damage now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:18:14-07:00","id":472897,"title":"","content":"They wait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:35:26-07:00","id":472917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/472827-2e-rites-questions?p=472897#post472897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They wait.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh, that's nasty. Though, admittedly, there are fewer sources of aggravated damage in all the 2nd edition games than before.<br /> <br /> Watch out that silverware, then!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:40:37-07:00","id":472924,"title":"","content":"They also heal aggravated about twice as fast as normal humans rather than at the same rate now. (four days vs a week)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:44:20-07:00","id":472931,"title":"","content":"Also, aggravated damage is supposed to be really nasty stuff. Sure, Uratha can heal from just about anything if they live through it, but aggravated damage means that large chunks of you are missing. Two weeks and two days to regrow a bitten-off leg seems like a sweet deal to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:45:46-07:00","id":472935,"title":"","content":"I didn't know about the aggravated healing speed. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:08:05-07:00","id":472979,"title":"","content":"Nothing actually prevents you from implementing rites from the old corebook in the new system, tho. Developers just didn't had the space to include everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}